# Constructions the Stop hook lets through. check-constructions.sh --soft
# prints only these, --hard prints the rest. A name is the text of a rule in
# banned-constructions.txt up to its first full stop, matched whole.
# prose-write.sh ignores this file, so a written file is still refused on
# every construction.
Negative incorporation on a determiner
Active clause with a pronominalised head
Active relative clause with a pronominalised head
Selectional restriction on the subject
Contrast coordinated with 'and'
Delexical verb
Unnamed document
Bare definite noun phrase
Verbless fragment after a comma
Wrong preposition: "at" for a thing that isn't a place
Contact clause with the head as its object
Selectional restriction: a card can't speak
Selectional restriction: "names" with a thing as its subject
Manner clause with "as" and a pronominalised object
Contact clause with a negated verb
Delexical "get" for a future passive
Present tense for work that will happen later
